          "note": "The complete new ordinary-arc proof of Theorem4.4 was read through Sections5–10, with the generalized tile definitions, matching statistics and elementary-lamination/shear conventions. It explicitly constructs the polygon lift when consecutive pending arcs occur, proves the quadrilateral/bigon crossing induction, defines and checks the specialization on first mutations, matches principal-coefficient exponents and transfers the ordinary polygon matching expansion. The standard surface polygon theorem and BFZ acyclic presentation are genuine prior background; the new orbifold steps are supplied. The critical construction/pentagon/lamination diagrams on physical pp.11,12,18,24,26 were rendered and inspected. Select ordinary non-self-intersecting arcs and orbifold orders >=3; generalized winding curves, closed band graphs and separate matrix formulas are not counted."
